src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol:checkReentrancyContext:156|class=C23|High|On any vault deployed with CurveInterface.V2, the hardcoded burn amount 1 in ICurve2TokenPoolV2(CURVE_POOL).remove_liquidity(1, minAmounts, true, address(this)) makes Curve call burnFrom(msg.sender = LP_LIB, 1) on a library that by construction holds zero LP tokens (all LP-handling entrypoints are delegatecalled into the vault), so the call underflows and reverts — bricking _checkReentrancyContext → _preLiquidation → the entire liquidation path, letting any unprivileged borrower hold a permanently unliquidatable underwater position.|src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol
